{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{g_i : T_i \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0008": "$T_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-refine-fppf-schemes}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7056d68bc16be1ff3e395e12f41cd985f28b987764b01f517f281e2565ad1b27", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0096d97af78754671f6e38c18cb85ac3319041ec74d25d52bd9d87ce62d29c4c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nSuppose that <MATH_0004> is an\nfppf covering of <MATH_0005>. Then there exists a refinement\n<MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007> which is an\nfppf covering such that each <MATH_0008> is a scheme.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3fb1aa919a780a594f5299d382bb57940dbd96fc61ec9f47dd1815896d3a8fd4", "unit_id": "tag:042T:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$i$", "MATH_0002": "$T_i$", "MATH_0003": "$T_i \\to X_i$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{T_i \\to X\\}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:76ba48cb1d3a0802761d7f08cf28b39bb1b90388d5378592d9b74e2632aa2504", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:66b771d73732cb1115870b39eec941f3962046bd3b4f51ae59159a46946a0ee4", "source_text": "Omitted. Hint: For each <MATH_0001> choose a scheme <MATH_0002> and a surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale\nmorphism <MATH_0003>. Then check that <MATH_0004> is an fppf covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6c86382908944cd93f5dada798ed06e2a762726142ce5b055db5f487ed4b7458", "unit_id": "tag:042T:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03Y7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\coprod X_i \\longrightarrow X\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fppf-covering-surjective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:98f6d8737e6f4b6448d7c933820dac883bf7c6ca059f0bb52685d610f5c08341", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d2234eba9317a6bbcc4e910564e391c400c5b4bb564de8e45f07b5b82f1c6c06", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an fppf covering of algebraic\nspaces over <MATH_0003>. Then the map of sheaves\n<MATH_0004>\nis surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:52676ab60754f627e980f3eb2aa135a08779278e44627aaabdda722a62305f1b", "unit_id": "tag:0469:statement"}
